    {
      "id": "cb5-l2",
      "title": "$ , and .",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "In an edited picture, the point is real: PIC ZZ9.99 prints the decimal point. A comma prints a comma, but only if there are digits before it.",
        "A $ at the front prints a dollar sign: PIC $Z,ZZ9.99 shows 1234.5 as $1,234.50. With several $ at the front, the sign floats to the first digit: PIC $$$,$$9.99 shows 12.5 as $12.50, with the spaces in front.",
        "Edited pictures are built symbol by symbol, so it's worth practicing: the exercises below let you build them yourself."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.",
          "       PROGRAM-ID. MONEY.",
          "       DATA DIVISION.",
          "       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.",
          "       01 AMOUNT     PIC 9(5)V99 VALUE 1234.5.",
          "       01 FIXED-OUT  PIC $ZZ,ZZ9.99.",
          "       01 FLOAT-OUT  PIC $$$,$$9.99.",
          "       PROCEDURE DIVISION.",
          "           MOVE AMOUNT TO FIXED-OUT FLOAT-OUT.",
          "           DISPLAY \"[\" FIXED-OUT \"]\".",
          "           DISPLAY \"[\" FLOAT-OUT \"]\".",
          "           STOP RUN."
        ],
        "output": [
          "[$ 1,234.50]",
          "[ $1,234.50]"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
