    {
      "id": "cb5-l3",
      "title": "Signs and Stars",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "An edited picture can show a sign. A - at the end (or the front) prints a minus for negative numbers and a space for positive ones; + always prints + or -.",
        "Accountants write CR (credit) after a negative amount: PIC ZZ9.99CR shows -5 as 5.00CR. DB (debit) works the same way.",
        "On cheques, empty places were dangerous: someone could write a 9 in front. So cheque printers used *: PIC ***9.99 fills them with stars: ***42.50."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.",
          "       PROGRAM-ID. CHEQUE.",
          "       DATA DIVISION.",
          "       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.",
          "       01 AMOUNT     PIC 9(4)V99  VALUE 42.5.",
          "       01 REFUND     PIC S9(4)V99 VALUE -12.",
          "       01 CHEQUE-OUT PIC **,**9.99.",
          "       01 CREDIT-OUT PIC Z,ZZ9.99CR.",
          "       01 MINUS-OUT  PIC -Z,ZZ9.99.",
          "       PROCEDURE DIVISION.",
          "           MOVE AMOUNT TO CHEQUE-OUT.",
          "           DISPLAY \"PAY \" CHEQUE-OUT.",
          "           MOVE REFUND TO CREDIT-OUT.",
          "           DISPLAY \"REFUND \" CREDIT-OUT.",
          "           MOVE REFUND TO MINUS-OUT.",
          "           DISPLAY \"REFUND \" MINUS-OUT.",
          "           STOP RUN."
        ],
        "output": [
          "PAY ****42.50",
          "REFUND    12.00CR",
          "REFUND -   12.00"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
